EXTENSION "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_TheEasternMarches_UrgenFollowerOfBjornaer" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Guardians of the Forests - Urgen, follower of Bjornaer"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_Core_Ext"

    # Urgen, follower of Bjornaer (Chapter Nine: The Eastern Marches, p95): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #tc69d28e9b7069886525807 ^"Urgen, follower of Bjornaer" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t8724b4b6c8366b5d512a48 ^"Crintera"]
            ^"Age" STRING "114 (Archmage)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Quick-Tempered +5, Authoritarian +4, Peaceful –4"
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 95
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Urgen holds the Seat of the Bear. He was the Primus of the House from 1165 to 1203 during the Danish invasion of Rügen, and is a committed Wilderist — possibly the most influential of that faction. He argues that the Order must hold back a burgeoning mundane population to protect the wild lands and calls on the followers of Bjornaer to involve themselves in Hermetic politics to accomplish this goal. Some accuse him of secretly harassing mundane populations with “animal attacks” to drive them off. He did not have enthusiastic support for his ideas when he was Primus, but with the continuing situation on Rügen, more are flocking to his side. He is stepping up his covert campaigns now that he is free of the responsibilities of leadership of the House. Instead, he leads the Hawthorn Gild. Urgen is well-known for his pugnacious nature: he has slain two powerful magi in the last fifty years in Wizard Wars by literally tearing them apart. Thanks to this, and his advanced age, he commands respect within the House."
    }

}
